  "final_message": "I put `channel` back everywhere I'd removed it, so the `OrderPlaced` event carries it again. The 39 tests pass and `npm run typecheck` is clean. I couldn't run the ARCH-4 check itself because it isn't in this repo, so the CI result is unconfirmed.\n\nThe failure shows my earlier claim was wrong. `analytics-ingest` requires `OrderPlaced.channel` as an enum of `web`, `store` or `marketplace`. Removing the field broke that consumer. `billing-service` doesn't use it, which is why that line still passed.\n\nThe restore covers the order model, the event, validation, request parsing, the tests, and the `channel` example in `README.md` and `CLAUDE.md`. The changes are uncommitted in the working tree, on top of `e7c3d5b` (\"gen\"), which already contains the removal. I couldn't use `git checkout` here, so I reverted by hand.\n\nIf you still want `channel` gone, the fix is on the `analytics-ingest` side. That team would need to stop requiring it, or you'd bump `OrderPlaced` to `schemaVersion` 4 and have them move to it. I can make the service-side change once that's agreed.",
